{"type":"text","timestamp":1794321314763,"sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","part":{"id":"prt_1c5e273bc001f13cLHoBDOw7XL","messageID":"msg_1c5e261cb001YAMO1b3qLXVVAB","sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait, there's a bug in the login function: I query `SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = ?` then separately fetch the password hash. That's convoluted and does two queries. Let me clean it up: fetch id and password_hash in one query.\n\nAlso in `seed_samples`, `created_at = connection.execute(...)` is assigned but only used as a None check — fine but awkward. Let me clean.\n\nAlso `connection.execute(\"BEGIN IMMEDIATE\")` — python sqlite3 with default isolation_level starts transactions implicitly; executing BEGIN IMMEDIATE while a transaction is open may error. Since `executescript` commits pending, then `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` should work. But careful: python's sqlite3 module in legacy mode auto-begins transactions before INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. Explicitly issuing BEGIN IMMEDIATE when no transaction is active is fine.\n\nLet me fix the login function and clean up seed_samples.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794321314748,"end":1794321314761}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794321314797,"sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_r4zm2aHTueBFEzZfPHZCEvmg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","newString":"row = get_db().execute(\n        \"SELECT id, password_hash FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is None or not check_password_hash(row[\"password_hash\"], password):\n        return api_error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n\n    return jsonify({\"token\": issue_token(row[\"id\"])})","oldString":"row = get_db().execute(\"SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)).fetchone()\n    if row is None or not check_password_hash(\n        get_db().execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],)).fetchone()[\"password_hash\"],\n        password,\n    ):\n        return api_error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n\n    return jsonify({\"token\": issue_token(row[\"id\"])})"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -451,13 +451,12 @@\n         \"username\": \"Username is required.\" if not username else \"\",\n         \"password\": \"Password is required.\" if not password else \"\",\n     })\n \n-row = get_db().execute(\"SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)).fetchone()\n-if row is None or not check_password_hash(\n-    get_db().execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],)).fetchone()[\"password_hash\"],\n-    password,\n-):\n+row = get_db().execute(\n+    \"SELECT id, password_hash FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)\n+).fetchone()\n+if row is None or not check_password_hash(row[\"password_hash\"], password):\n     return api_error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n \n return jsonify({\"token\": issue_token(row[\"id\"])})\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/app.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -451,13 +451,12 @@\n         \"username\": \"Username is required.\" if not username else \"\",\n         \"password\": \"Password is required.\" if not password else \"\",\n     })\n \n-row = get_db().execute(\"SELECT id FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)).fetchone()\n-if row is None or not check_password_hash(\n-    get_db().execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],)).fetchone()[\"password_hash\"],\n-    password,\n-):\n+row = get_db().execute(\n+    \"SELECT id, password_hash FROM users WHERE username = ?\", (username,)\n+).fetchone()\n+if row is None or not check_password_hash(row[\"password_hash\"], password):\n     return api_error(\"Incorrect username or password.\", 401)\n \n return jsonify({\"token\": issue_token(row[\"id\"])})\n \n","additions":4,"deletions":5},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794321314757,"end":1794321314773}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c5e273be001xUzZslQbJONEFf","sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","messageID":"msg_1c5e261cb001YAMO1b3qLXVVAB"}}
