{"type":"text","timestamp":1794321560528,"sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","part":{"id":"prt_1c5e633c2001isKTtGbuyYjTCL","messageID":"msg_1c5e625b7001jCXvSN1V3RD78F","sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","type":"text","text":"<think>I have `readStoredUser` unused. I should use it as a fallback for the initial user state (before /me resolves) so the header shows the username immediately. Let me use it in useState initializer:\n\n```tsx\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<AuthUser | null>(() => readStoredUser());\n```\n\nThat's better UX: the header shows the username right away. But then if the token is invalid, /me fails and we clear. Fine.\n\nCareful: the `ready` flag remains false until the /me check completes. But if there's no token, ready = true.\n\nLet me apply.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794321560514,"end":1794321560526}}}
