{"type":"text","timestamp":1794321605448,"sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","part":{"id":"prt_1c5e6e338001d8oqdwkHDMntYd","messageID":"msg_1c5e6d272001gwhOl8rcvgJ4PT","sessionID":"ses_e3a21d981ffebd45Va6soahg7t","type":"text","text":"<think>Playwright is available in the registry. Installing the browser binary requires downloading from playwright's CDN (https://playwright.azureedge.net or cdn.playwright.dev) which is likely blocked (no other network access). Let me try installing playwright-core + chromium via npm... The `playwright` npm package downloads browsers on install via `npx playwright install`, which fetches from the CDN. The npm package itself contains a browser download URL; the sandbox may have a proxy for it.\n\nLet me try: `npm install -D playwright@1.65.0` then `npx playwright install chromium --with-deps`? The --with-deps needs apt (root). Let me just try `npx playwright install chromium` and see if it can download.\n\nThis is worth ~2 minutes to validate the UI renders. Let me try.\n\nActually, let me be careful not to pollute the frontend package.json with playwright (it would end up in package-lock.json and the Docker build). I'll install it in a separate temp directory outside the workspace... but /tmp/opencode isn't writable. Hmm, it said \"Permission denied\" for /tmp/opencode writes. Let me check if I can write to /tmp directly (e.g., /tmp/pwtest).\n\nActually the pip cache is at /tmp/llmlab-deps/pip, so /tmp is writable? Let me test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794321605432,"end":1794321605445}}}
